Apple today announced that select <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/home/accessories/apple-home-collection">Apple Home Collection accessories</a> will be available to order starting Friday, November 13, with availability beginning in December. Apple did not say exactly which accessories can be ordered tomorrow, so stay tuned.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-home-collection-feature2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070669" /><br/>
Introduced alongside Apple's new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-announces-homeview-smart-home-hub/">HomeView</a> smart home hub last month, the Apple Home Collection is a new lineup of smart home accessories that LG and Schneider Electric designed in collaboration with Apple. There are indoor and outdoor cameras, thermostats, temperature sensors, a video doorbell, and a door lock.<br/>
<br/>
All of the Apple Home Collection accessories work with the HomeView:<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Video Doorbell (&#36;249.95)</strong> - The Video Doorbell has dual cameras that capture views of visitors and packages. The front camera has a 2.5K resolution and the bottom camera is full HD resolution. It has a built-in spotlight and a chime that plays through HomeView, HomePod, or HomePod mini.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Outdoor Cam (&#36;299.95)</strong> - The Outdoor Cam has low-light color night vision and can be angled in multiple positions.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Indoor Cam (&#36;199.95)</strong> - The Indoor Cam has a privacy-preserving feature that allows it to tilt up when people are in the home so it's not recording, and down when people leave for keeping an eye on the home. The tilt function works based on geofencing, but can also be controlled in the Home app or manually.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Floodlight Cam (&#36;399.95)</strong> - The Floodlight Cam has dual floodlights that activate when motion is detected and low-light color night vision.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Smart Deadbolt Lock (&#36;349.95)</strong> - The lock has Ultra Wideband and can unlock automatically when the homeowner approaches, with no tap required. It also supports unlocking via PIN or a hidden backup key slot, and there is detection for whether the door is opened, closed, or has been tampered with. The doorbell and lock can work together as one, letting users see who is at the door and unlocking it if needed.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Thermostat (&#36;199.95)</strong> - The thermostat supports Adaptive Temperature and in the U.S., heating and cooling can be activated during lower-cost periods for users with a compatible utility plan. The thermostat can read temperature and humidity across multiple rooms using separate temperature and humidity sensors. Sensors are priced at &#36;39.95.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Schneider Electric Thermostat (&#36;199.95)</strong> - Also supports Adaptive Temperature and can be used with temperature and humidity sensors. Sensors are priced at &#36;39.95.</li><br/>
</ul>For more details about the accessories, read <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-home-collection/">our previous coverage</a>.<br/>
